==English==

===Verb===
'''[[have]] a [[ball]]'''

# {{idiomatic}} To [[enjoy]] thoroughly; to have lots of [[fun]] or [[excitement]].
#: ''The kids '''had a ball''' playing in the fountain.''
#* '''1973''', [[w:Slade (band)|Slade]] - ''[[w:Merry Xmas Everybody|Merry Xmas Everybody]]''
#*: Are you hanging up a stocking on your wall?
#*: It's the time that every Santa '''has a ball'''
#*: Does he ride a red-nosed reindeer?
#*: Does a ton up on his sleigh
#*: Do the fairies keep him sober for a day?
#* '''1976''', [[w:ABBA|ABBA]] - ''[[w:Money, Money, Money|Money]]''
#*: In my dreams I have a plan
#*: If I got me a wealthy man
#*: I wouldn't have to work at all, I'd fool around and '''have a ball'''
#*'''1998''', [[w:Baha Men|Baha Men]] - ''[[w:Who Let the Dogs Out?|Who Let the Dogs Out?]]''
#*:''When the party was nice, the party was jumpin' (Hey, Yippie, Yi, Yo)''
#*:''And everybody havin' a ball (Hah, ho, Yippie Yi Yo)''''

